Thanks again Fausto,

I really appreciate your help.

I can see how your code works, and also it should be possible to do the
exact same thing with amixer. However I have noticed that I can only control
some of the "simple mixer controls" in a mixer but not all of them. It
appears I can control the simple mixer controls that have "volume"
capability, but I cannot control simple mixer controls with the pvolume,
pswitch, cvolume, cswitch etc.

The command I use is this: amixer -c 0 cset name='Ext Mic Boost' 0


but if I try
amixer -c 0 cset name='Capture' 1

I get the following error

amixer: Cannot find the given element from control hw:0

I have attached the also-info.txt for my machine to this mail.



